Notebook[{Cell["TMD beam and soft functions, step 4: the NLO soft function", 
   "Title"], Cell["Input: Results/<route>/Algebra.wl (step 2) and \
Results/Integrals.wl (step 3).  Output: Results/<route>/Soft.wl with the bare \
and the renormalized NLO soft function for quarks and gluons, compared with \
Luo, Yang, Zhu and Zhu, arXiv:2012.03256.\n\nThe soft function S_i(b, mu, nu) \
= (1/N_i) <0| Tr[...] |0> is 1 at lowest order.  At NLO the real emission of \
one gluon from the two Wilson lines gives, with the squared current of step \
2, M2_s = 4 gs^2 C_i/((n.k)(nb.k)), and the phase space and regulator of step \
3,\n\n   S_i^(1),bare = 4 C_i as T[2 K0(2 a kT)],\n\nwhere T[2 K0] is the \
soft master integral of step 3.  Virtual corrections are scaleless and \
vanish.  The renormalized soft function is obtained by minimal subtraction of \
the poles: S_i^(1) = finite part of S_i^(1),bare.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Load", "Section"], Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \
\"..\", \"..\", \"FeynFacet\", \"FeynFacet.wl\"}]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["route = \"FeynCalc\";\nalgebra = LoadResult[\"Algebra\", \
route];\nintegrals = LoadResult[\"Integrals\"];\nalgebra[\"Soft\"]", 
   "Input"], Cell["From the squared current to the bare soft function", 
   "Section"], Cell["Phase space (step 3): d^D k/(2 Pi)^(D-1) delta+(k^2) = \
d^{D-2}kT d(n.k)/(2 (n.k) (2 Pi)^(D-1)) with (n.k)(nb.k) = kT2.  Hence\n\n   \
S^(1) = Integral d^{D-2}kT/(2 Pi)^(D-2) e^{i b.kT} [M2_s kT2/gs^2] gs^2/(4 Pi \
kT2) Integral dy/y R(y, kT)   (y = n.k),\n\nand with gs^2 = 16 Pi^2 as muR^(2 \
eps) (e^EulerGamma/(4 Pi))^eps and the definition of T[f] (which contains 4 \
Pi muR^(2 eps) (e^EulerGamma/(4 Pi))^eps): S^(1) = as [M2_s kT2/gs^2] \
T[Integral dy/y R].  The bracket is the colour factor 4 C_i, and the \
regulated longitudinal integral is 2 K0(2 a kT).", "Text"], 
  Cell["colourFactor = Map[Simplify[# kn kb/gs^2] &, \
algebra[\"Soft\"]];\nRequire[colourFactor === <|\"q\" -> 4 CF, \"g\" -> 4 \
CA|>, \"Unexpected soft colour factors\", colourFactor];\nsoftBare = \
Map[Collect[# as integrals[\"SoftMaster\"], {as, eps}, Simplify] &, \
colourFactor]", "Input"], Cell["Poles: 4 C_i/eps^2 - 4 C_i Lv/eps (the double \
pole is the cusp, the single pole carries the rapidity logarithm).", "Text"], 
  Cell["poles = Map[{Coefficient[#, eps, -2], Coefficient[#, eps, -1]} &, \
softBare];\nRequire[Simplify[poles[\"q\"] - {4 CF as, -4 CF as Lv}] === {0, \
0} && Simplify[poles[\"g\"] - {4 CA as, -4 CA as Lv}] === {0, 0},\n  \
\"Unexpected poles of the bare soft function\", poles];\npoles", "Input"], 
  Cell["Renormalized soft function and comparison", "Section"], 
  Cell["soft = Map[Simplify[Coefficient[#, eps, 0]] &, softBare]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"reference\", \
\"Luo2020.wl\"}]];\nreference = Luo2020NLO[x, Lp, LQ, Lv, Lh, CF, CA, TF] /. \
zeta[2] -> Zeta[2];\ndifference = Map[Simplify[soft[#]/as - \
reference[\"Soft\"][#]] &, <|\"q\" -> \"q\", \"g\" -> \"g\"|>]", "Input"], 
  Cell["result = <|\"SoftBare\" -> softBare, \"Soft\" -> soft, \
\"LiteratureDifference\" -> difference, \"Route\" -> \
route|>;\nSaveResult[\"Soft\", result, route];\nRequire[difference === \
<|\"q\" -> 0, \"g\" -> 0|>, \"The soft function differs from \
arXiv:2012.03256\", difference];\nsoft", "Input"]}, WindowSize -> {1000, 800}]
